Package: rflpSNP
Title: In Silico Design and Simulation of PCR-RFLP Assays for SNP Genotyping
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Miguel", "Esparza", , "esparzamiguel057@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools to design PCR-RFLP primers from a reference sequence in
    FASTA format and a dbSNP flanking sequence, evaluate physicochemical
    properties (Tm, %GC, dimers and hairpins), simulate the PCR in silico on
    the reference sequence, locate the cut site of a restriction enzyme in
    the resulting amplicon, and simulate the expected band pattern on an
    agarose gel for the three possible genotypes (homozygous uncut,
    heterozygous and homozygous cut). Intended as a teaching and
    reproducibility tool for the design of PCR-RFLP genotyping assays.
